  "notes": "{終|お}える means to finish or complete something. It is a transitive verb that takes を.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {終|お}わる (intransitive — something ends by itself)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{終|お}えている means \"have finished\" — the resulting state after completing something.\n\nCOMPOUND VERB PATTERN:\nVerb stem + {終|お}える means \"to finish doing ~\":\n- {読|よ}み{終|お}える: to finish reading\n- {食|た}べ{終|お}える: to finish eating\n- {書|か}き{終|お}える: to finish writing\n- {片|かた}づけ{終|お}える: to finish tidying up\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {終|お}わる: to end (intransitive — the event/task itself ends)\n- {済|す}ませる: to get something done with (implies completing a task or obligation)\n- {終了|しゅうりょう}する: to conclude, to end (formal, often for events or systems)",
